Record the microphone through macOS voice processing, so it cancels echo.

The sound of a call that the server plays from this Mac's speakers reached the
microphone again, and everyone else in the call heard themselves with a strong
delay. FreeRDP recorded through a plain AudioQueue. Now it records through
Apple's VoiceProcessingIO unit (FaceTime's echo cancellation, noise
suppression and gain control), with ducking of other sound turned down to the
minimum. If the unit cannot start, the old AudioQueue recorder is used.

